Fix SEL RTAC parsing of project exports. Before, the parse of a directory failed with ``AttributeError`` for 5 of 6 public project exports, because PEAT expected ``<ArchivedContent>`` in every POU (for tarballs, PEAT logged an error for each POU and dropped the logic). Also, one file that couldn't be parsed stopped the parse of a directory, non-XML files in a tarball caused a ``UnicodeDecodeError``, access point routers stored XML elements instead of text, cells that are read-only in the editor (``enabled="false"``) were dropped, a task without a name in ``Main Controller.xml`` was stored under the key ``None``, and tarball members with ``..`` in the path could be written outside of the device's output directory.
